@cc [owner:spolu,label:security] v3-tenant-isolation
Persistent keys, cache entries, and grant decisions MUST be tenant-scoped. Filesystem requests
MUST derive the tenant and at most 512 grants from an authenticated active session.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:concurrency] v3-object-consistency
Each bounded operation MUST expose one coherent object state. Size, blocks, parent links,
namespace entries, and grant indexes MUST change atomically in RAM and in FDB as applicable.
Independent object edits MUST NOT be combined into one FDB transaction. Namespace operations
MUST coordinate exactly their participating objects, including a replacement victim.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:backend] v3-ram-acknowledgment
Filesystem mutations and fsync MUST acknowledge complete server RAM acceptance without awaiting
FDB commit. Already known publication errors MUST reach subsequent fsyncs/mutations. Successful
fsync MAY be lost on crash. Restart MUST recover only committed FDB state.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:concurrency] v3-independent-writers
FDB conflict validation MUST provide cross-server correctness. Tenant affinity MUST NOT imply
exclusive ownership. No tenant lock may be held over publication I/O. Ambiguous mutations MUST
NOT be automatically replayed.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:performance;security] v3-bounded-freshness
Publication delay P and read/authority cache age C MUST satisfy P + C <= D, initially D = 1000 ms.
RPC delivery is outside D. Hits and later writes MUST NOT extend expiry or publication deadlines.
Expired views MUST refresh or fail. Dirty state and cache memory MUST be bounded.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:architecture] v3-uncached-client
The FUSE client MUST use direct I/O, zero metadata/name TTLs, and no kernel writeback or retained
userspace data, xattr, or directory-page cache. Clients MUST NOT send expected object versions.
Read responses MUST carry size and bytes from the same state. Each RPC carries at most 1 MiB I/O.
